# Backpack (polyfills:backpack) — item behavior example.
#
# Right-click opens a 2-page menu built from the SAME pages[] system machines use (see
# items/backpack.json) — free "storage" slots plus a next/prev button pair, not a plain chest.
# Shift-right-click on a block face places `polyfills:storage_block` and spills every page's
# stored contents straight into it (see DataItemBehavior#tryPlaceContainerBlock); this script then
# runs once the block is down, with `item` (the backpack, still holding its old NBT) and `Block`
# (the freshly placed block) both bound.

def on_place_block():
    Player.send_message("<green>Backpack unpacked into a storage block.")
end

# storage_filter's `script` — the id-list `deny` in the JSON already blocks a backpack/jetpack
# nesting inside itself; this adds a second, script-driven rule as a worked example of the
# "or a script function" filter form: refuse anything enchanted (nothing sensible fits in a bag
# that isn't also just a plain resource). Runs for EVERY attempted placement into a storage slot,
# with `item` bound to the candidate being placed (not the backpack itself).
def can_store(item):
    if item.enchantments.size > 0:
        Player.send_message("<red>That won't fit — enchanted items stay out of the backpack.")
        return false
    end
    return true
end



